# FP-reasoning: MEDIUM, network_mode=any (pure L3/L4 — SSH is encrypted but the
# CONNECTION RATE is visible without decryption). NON-payload class (spec §22 C1):
# no fast_pattern; decisive condition = repeated to_server SYN to tcp/22 from one
# src. threshold count 20/60s by_src is the FP compensator: legitimate SSH users
# reconnect occasionally; 20 new connections/60s from one src to 22 is brute/spray.
# Residual FP: CI runners / bastions doing many short SSH sessions -> tune via
# threshold.config suppress for known hosts (NOT deprecation). Negative exercises
# the decisive condition: 5 SYN to tcp/22 (normal admin) -> below threshold -> silent.
alert tcp any any -> any 22 (msg:"REDAC7D BRUTEFORCE SSH - high connection rate to tcp/22 from one source [medium]"; flow:to_server; flags:S,12; threshold:type threshold, track by_src, count 20, seconds 60; classtype:attempted-recon; metadata: asset_category infra, owasp none, attack_target Server, mitre_tactic_id TA0006, mitre_tactic_name Credential-Access, mitre_technique_id T1110, mitre_technique_name Brute-Force, kill_chain Exploitation, confidence medium, signature_severity Major, deployment Perimeter, network_mode any, cve none, poc_ref tests/poc/9430001_ssh-connrate/poc.sh, tag ssh-bruteforce, created_at 2026_05_18, updated_at 2026_05_18, author redac7d; sid:9430001; rev:1;)
